        <h1>From Web to Mobile</h1>
        <h2 class="text-center mb-4">Martin Medina</h2>

        <section>
            <h2>Honors Project</h2>

            <p class="bio">
                "From Web to Mobile: Enhancing a Full-Stack Job Application
                Tracker for Smartphone Users" is the honors extension of the
                Job Application Tracker project.
            </p>

            <p class="bio">
                This project explores how a mobile-first redesign can improve
                the usability and efficiency of a job application tracker.
                Since job seekers may research positions, submit applications,
                and check updates on their phones, the interface should remain
                clear and convenient on smaller screens.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Mobile Development Focus</h2>

            <ul>
                <li>Mobile-first design and responsive layouts.</li>
                <li>Navigation that works on small screens.</li>
                <li>Touch-friendly buttons and controls.</li>
                <li>Forms that are easy to complete on smartphones.</li>
                <li>Readable application details and status information.</li>
                <li>Usability testing and improvements based on feedback.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Planned Mobile Features</h2>

            <ul>
                <li><strong>Quick Add Application:</strong> A simplified way to record a job opportunity.</li>
                <li><strong>Application Status Timeline:</strong> A clear view of application progress.</li>
                <li><strong>Interview and Follow-Up Reminders:</strong> Easier access to important dates.</li>
                <li><strong>Priority Applications:</strong> A way to highlight opportunities needing attention.</li>
                <li><strong>Mobile Search and Filtering:</strong> A simpler way to locate saved applications.</li>
            </ul>

            <p class="bio">
                These features are proposed enhancements and will be evaluated
                as the honors project develops.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section>
            <h2>Testing and Evaluation</h2>

            <p class="bio">
                The mobile design will be reviewed at different screen sizes
                and in supported browsers. Volunteer users may be asked to
                complete common tasks, such as adding an application, updating
                its status, locating an important opportunity, and navigating
                the interface. Their feedback will help identify usability
                issues and guide further improvements.
            </p>
        </section>

